          "articleText": "Benchmarks Nifty22,421.95-198.5FEATURED FUNDS★★★★★Motilal Oswal Midcap Fund Direct-Growth5Y Return19.6 % Invest NowEnter search text:Benchmarks Nifty22,421.95-198.5FEATURED FUNDS★★★★★Motilal Oswal Midcap Fund Direct-Growth5Y Return19.6 % Invest NowEnter search text:Business News›News›Elections›Assembly Elections UP elections: Akhilesh Yadav in talks with many BJP MLAs, working to accommodate themSamajwadi Party chief Akhilesh Yadav indicated that several BJP MLAs are in contact with his party. He mentioned the challenges in accommodating these MLAs within the party structure. Yadav stated that the SP plans to maintain largely the same allies for the upcoming Uttar Pradesh elections. The Congress party is also seeking unity among opposition factions to address electoral concerns.CM Adityanath says 'Ramdrohi' will create confusion over Sanatan glory, calls for unityUttar Pradesh Chief Minister Yogi Adityanath addressed a gathering at Gorakhnath temple on Ram temple construction. He emphasized the significance of unity among followers of Sanatan Dharma traditions and sects. Adityanath recalled the involvement of Mahant Digvijay Nath in the Ram Janmabhoomi movement and the strategy behind Ram Lalla's installation. He warned against those creating confusion regarding the glory of Lord Ram and Sanatan Dharma.SP's 27,000-per-seat push takes it to north's 'dalit capital' AgraThe party is also looking to attract Dalit voters apparently drifting away from the Bahujan Samaj Party (BSP) and will hold a SC conference in Agra, the Dalit capital of north India, on November 15. \"I have been touring West UP to invite SC voters and am in touch with local organisations to ensure a massive gathering. We will tell voters that BJP does not have SC voters' interests in mind,\" SP's national general secretary Ramji Lal Suman told ET on phone.Ayodhya to Mathura: BJP's new poll hubThe assembly elections will be the first election in the state where the construction of the Ram Temple in Ayodhya will not be an election issue, as the temple has been constructed. A few UP BJP leaders told ET that the party now wants to take its campaign beyond Ayodhya, especially after the recent incident of donation theft in the temple.Even if we win all seats, we are against EVMs: Akhilesh YadavMayawati demands return to ballot papers, says EVMs undermine trust in electionsUproar over SIR unfortunate, says Yogi Aditynath; demands apology from Congress, alliesAAP turned Punjab into 'Udta Punjab', BJP will make it 'Ubharda Punjab': Pushkar Singh DhamiBJP's UP poll blueprint: Fresh faces, joint decision-making and winnability2027 Assembly battle: Drugs top Opposition poll issue in PunjabVoter list row: 3.27 crore new electors aged 18-28 added since June 2025; EC explains new declaration rule for Form 6AAP alleges Centre misusing agencies ahead of assembly polls amid ED searches in PunjabAkhilesh Yadav slams 'bulldozer action' in Ayodhya, promises compensation if Samajwadi Party returns to powerUP elections: Akhilesh Yadav in talks with many BJP MLAs, working to accommodate themSamajwadi Party chief Akhilesh Yadav indicated that several BJP MLAs are in contact with his party. He mentioned the challenges in accommodating these MLAs within the party structure. Yadav stated that the SP plans to maintain largely the same allies for the upcoming Uttar Pradesh elections. The Congress party is also seeking unity among opposition factions to address electoral concerns.Uttar PradeshUttar PradeshUP elections: Akhilesh Yadav in talks with many BJP MLAs, working to accommodate themSamajwadi Party chief Akhilesh Yadav indicated that several BJP MLAs are in contact with his party. He mentioned the challenges in accommodating these MLAs within the party structure. Yadav stated that the SP plans to maintain largely the same allies for the upcoming Uttar Pradesh elections. The Congress party is also seeking unity among opposition factions to address electoral conce