ive investment fund (AIF) focused on secured real estate debt opportunities across Delhi-NCR and West Bengal.The Poddar Keventer Real Estate Fund – Scheme I has a greenshoe option of ₹200 crore, taking its potential corpus to ₹600 crore. The sponsors have committed ₹80 crore, equivalent to 20% of the target corpus.The fund is targeting a gross internal rate of return (IRR) of 18-22% before expenses, according to the company.It plans to provide structured financing to ultra-luxury, premium and mid-market real estate projects. Investments will be structured through secured debt with security cover, escrow mechanisms, covenants and milestone-linked disbursements. By Online Bureau , ETRealty Published On Oct 3, 2026 at 08:45 AM IST See more on: Saroj Poddar Group, Keventer Group, Poddar Keventer Capital Advisors, Poddar Keventer Real Estate Fund, Category II alternative investment fund, Delhi-NCR, West Bengal Join the community of 2M+ industry professionals. Subscribe to Newsletter to get latest insights & analysis",
