          "title": "Uttar Pradesh: UPPCB puts up 90 cameras to check dust-control measures at construction sites",
          "description": "UPPCB installs 90 PTZ cameras at Noida construction sites to monitor dust-control measures, enforce NGT norms, and curb winter smog with CAQM oversight.",
          "articleText": "infrastructure 1 min read Uttar Pradesh: UPPCB puts up 90 cameras to check dust-control measures at construction sites To tackle the escalating pollution levels at construction sites in Noida, the Uttar Pradesh Pollution Control Board has initiated a surveillance program featuring camera installations at 90 construction locations. This step not only aligns with the National Green Tribunal’s dust-control mandates but also urges developers to comply with environmental standards. A dedicated control room will soon monitor the success and application of these dust management measures. TN Mohammed Ishan TNN Published On Oct 2, 2026 at 09:49 AM IST Representative AI imageNOIDA: Uttar Pradesh Pollution Control Board (UPPCB) has installed cameras at 90 construction sites across Noida to monitor dust-control measures, including installation of water sprinklers, anti-smog guns and wind-breaking walls, as a part of its efforts to check winter smog.“We have surveyed the sites and are now putting up PTZ cameras for surveillance. Cameras are already in place at 90 sites, and we will continue to add more. A control room is also being set up with CAQM in Delhi to monitor dust mitigation measures,” an UPPCB official said, adding that developers have been sent notices to adhere to NGT guidelines. Advt As per the guidelines laid down by the tribunal, builders should put up green barriers and wind-breaking walls around construction sites, keep construction material, such as sand, gravel and cement, covered, keep construction waste covered, install sprinklers to settle dust and provide masks and gloves to construction workers.Commission for Air Quality Management (CAQM) has also directed that anti-smog guns should be installed at construction sites in proportion to the built-up area — from at least one anti-smog gun for every 5,000 to 10,000 sqm to four for projects above 20,000 sqm.At J Kumar Infra Projects, which is completing a residential project in Sector 76, safety department official Vipin Kumar Yadav said a sprinkler sprays the tyres of every vehicle leaving the site. “A tanker is kept on the premises, and the whole site is sprinkled three to four times a day to keep dust down,” he said. Another official from the company said an anti-smog gun was deployed at the site’s entrance. By TN Mohammed Ishan , TNN Published On Oct 2, 2026 at 09:49 AM IST See more on: Uttar Pradesh Pollution Control Board, Noida, construction sites, PTZ cameras, dust-control measures, National Green Tribunal guidelines, Commission for Air Quality Management, anti-smog guns Join the community of 2M+ industry professionals. Subscribe to Newsletter to get latest insights & analysis in your inbox. All about ETRealty industry right on your smartphone! Download the ETRealty App and get the Realtime updates and Save your favourite articles. HomeNewsInfrastructureUttar Pradesh: UPPCB puts up 90 cameras to check dust-control measures at construction sites infrastructure 1 min read Uttar Pradesh: UPPCB puts up 90 cameras to check dust-control measures at construction sites To tackle the escalating pollution levels at construction sites in Noida, the Uttar Pradesh Pollution Control Board has initiated a surveillance program featuring camera installations at 90 construction locations. This step not only aligns with the National Green Tribunal’s dust-control mandates but also urges developers to comply with environmental standards. A dedicated control room will soon monitor the success and application of these dust management measures. infrastructure 1 min read TN Mohammed Ishan TNN Published On Oct 2, 2026 at 09:49 AM IST Representative AI imageNOIDA: Uttar Pradesh Pollution Control Board (UPPCB) has installed cameras at 90 construction sites across Noida to monitor dust-control measures, including installation of water sprinklers, anti-smog guns and wind-breaking walls, as a part of its efforts to check winter smog.“We have surveyed the sites and are 