          "title": "Kochi metro phase-II construction to be completed in August 2027",
          "description": "Kochi Metro Phase II from Kaloor to Kakkanad SmartCity targets completion by Aug 2027; KMRL reviews works, land acquisition, revenues and hiring.",
          "articleText": "infrastructure 1 min read Kochi metro phase-II construction to be completed in August 2027 Kochi Metro Rail Ltd is determined to complete its Phase II expansion by August 2027. Managing director G Priyanka stressed the critical need for swift progress on construction. The review covered vital components like track laying, station development, and electrical installations. KMRL aims to boost its finances by introducing new commercial strategies and filling essential positions. Times News Network TNN Published On Oct 2, 2026 at 03:00 PM IST KOCHI: Kochi Metro Rail Ltd (KMRL) has stepped up efforts to complete its Phase II expansion on schedule, said managing director G Priyanka, who chaired a comprehensive review meeting on Thursday to assess the construction progress.The Phase II alignment stretches from Jawaharlal Nehru Stadium in Kaloor to Kakkanad SmartCity, with the deadline revised to Aug 2027. The review covered track laying, station construction, electrical systems, lifts, escalators, signalling, telecommunications and automatic fare collection installations.Civil work on the remaining stretches will begin immediately as land acquisition on the right side of Palarivattom and Padamugal reaches completion. Advt KMRL plans to increase non-fare revenues alongside ticket sales to boost overall financial performance. Strategies include selling semi-naming rights for stations and launching new commercial initiatives as the Phase II line opens.The management also prioritised immediate recruitment for key vacant posts within the organisation to support these developments.Beyond the main Metro line, KMRL reviewed related infrastructure projects. Construction of the Water Metro stations at Kadamakkudy and Paliyamthuruth has reached its final stage, while progress continues on the Sreekaryam Flyover project in Thiruvananthapuram.“Intensive measures will be taken to complete the Phase II line on time,” Priyanka said after the meeting. By Times News Network , TNN Published On Oct 2, 2026 at 03:00 PM IST See more on: Kochi Metro Rail Ltd (KMRL), G Priyanka, Phase II expansion, Jawaharlal Nehru Stadium Kaloor, Kakkanad SmartCity, Water Metro stations, Sreekaryam Flyover Thiruvananthapuram, Kochi Join the community of 2M+ industry professionals. Subscribe to Newsletter to get latest insights & analysis in your inbox. All about ETRealty industry right on your smartphone! Download the ETRealty App and get the Realtime updates and Save your favourite articles. HomeNewsInfrastructureKochi metro phase-II construction to be completed in August 2027 infrastructure 1 min read Kochi metro phase-II construction to be completed in August 2027 Kochi Metro Rail Ltd is determined to complete its Phase II expansion by August 2027. Managing director G Priyanka stressed the critical need for swift progress on construction. The review covered vital components like track laying, station development, and electrical installations. KMRL aims to boost its finances by introducing new commercial strategies and filling essential positions. infrastructure 1 min read Times News Network TNN Published On Oct 2, 2026 at 03:00 PM IST KOCHI: Kochi Metro Rail Ltd (KMRL) has stepped up efforts to complete its Phase II expansion on schedule, said managing director G Priyanka, who chaired a comprehensive review meeting on Thursday to assess the construction progress.The Phase II alignment stretches from Jawaharlal Nehru Stadium in Kaloor to Kakkanad SmartCity, with the deadline revised to Aug 2027. The review covered track laying, station construction, electrical systems, lifts, escalators, signalling, telecommunications and automatic fare collection installations.Civil work on the remaining stretches will begin immediately as land acquisition on the right side of Palarivattom and Padamugal reaches completion. Advt KMRL plans to increase non-fare revenues alongside ticket sales to boost overall financial performance. Strategies include selling semi