          "title": "Trichy civic body warns builders over illegal construction & demolition waste dumping",
          "description": "Trichy Corporation warns builders against illegal C&D waste dumping on roads and near water bodies, will levy spot penalties and plans a Panjapur recycling unit.",
          "articleText": "infrastructure 1 min read Trichy civic body warns builders over illegal construction & demolition waste dumping Trichy corporation commissioner N Ponmalai has issued a stern warning to builders concerning the illegal dumping of construction materials, responding to rising public grievances. He emphasized that penalties will be enforced on offenders disrupting traffic, particularly in areas like Thennur and Vayalur Road. The commissioner reminded all sites to comply with guidelines and exhibit necessary approvals. As a proactive measure, a C&D waste recycling unit is planned for Panjapur. TNN Published On Oct 2, 2026 at 01:00 PM IST Representative AI imageTRICHY: Trichy corporation commissioner N Ponmalai on Thursday warned builders and construction companies against dumping construction and demolition (C&D) waste on roads and near water bodies, following complaints from residents that such dumping was affecting vehicular movement.The commissioner said penalties would be levied on the spot, as per the corporation’s bylaws, against those continuing to dispose of C&D waste illegally.Dumping of construction materials and debris on roads has caused traffic bottlenecks in several parts of the city, including Thennur, Vayalur Road and Uyyakondan aqueduct bund roads. The corporation also said temporary shelters for storing construction materials or accommodating workers should be confined to the private property where construction is under way and should not encroach on roads. Advt “Construction sites should display their building plans and approval details on boards. If any complaints are received from the public, we would inspect and levy appropriate penalties,” Ponmalai said.Builders and real estate developers requiring bulk disposal of C&D waste can approach ward- or zonal-level officers to facilitate safe disposal, the corporation said.As a long-term solution, the civic body plans to develop a C&D waste recycling unit at Panjapur on about four acres, along with collection points at multiple locations in the city. TNN Published On Oct 2, 2026 at 01:00 PM IST See more on: Trichy Corporation, N Ponmalai, construction and demolition waste, Thennur, Vayalur Road, Uyyakondan aqueduct bund, Panjapur, C&D waste recycling unit, Trichy Join the community of 2M+ industry professionals. Subscribe to Newsletter to get latest insights & analysis in your inbox. All about ETRealty industry right on your smartphone! Download the ETRealty App and get the Realtime updates and Save your favourite articles. HomeNewsInfrastructureTrichy civic body warns builders over illegal construction & demolition waste dumping infrastructure 1 min read Trichy civic body warns builders over illegal construction & demolition waste dumping Trichy corporation commissioner N Ponmalai has issued a stern warning to builders concerning the illegal dumping of construction materials, responding to rising public grievances. He emphasized that penalties will be enforced on offenders disrupting traffic, particularly in areas like Thennur and Vayalur Road. The commissioner reminded all sites to comply with guidelines and exhibit necessary approvals. As a proactive measure, a C&D waste recycling unit is planned for Panjapur. infrastructure 1 min read TNN Published On Oct 2, 2026 at 01:00 PM IST Representative AI imageTRICHY: Trichy corporation commissioner N Ponmalai on Thursday warned builders and construction companies against dumping construction and demolition (C&D) waste on roads and near water bodies, following complaints from residents that such dumping was affecting vehicular movement.The commissioner said penalties would be levied on the spot, as per the corporation’s bylaws, against those continuing to dispose of C&D waste illegally.Dumping of construction materials and debris on roads has caused traffic bottlenecks in several parts of the city, including Thennur, Vayalur Road and Uyyakondan aqueduct bund roads. The corporation also said temporary shelters for storing construction materials or accommodating workers should be confined to the private property where construction is under way and should not encroach on roads. Advt “Construction sites should display their building plans and approval details on boards. If any complaints are received from the public, we would inspect and levy appropriate penalties,” Ponmalai said.Builders and real estate developers requiring bulk disposal of C&D waste can approach ward- or zonal-level officers to facilitate safe disposal, the corporation said.As a long-term solution, the civic body plans to develop a C&D waste recycling unit at Panjapur on about four acres, along with collection points at multiple locations in the city. TNN Published On Oct 2, 2026 at 01:00 PM IST See more on: Trichy Corporation, N Ponmalai, construction and demolition waste, Thennur, Vayalur Road, Uyyakondan aqueduct bund, Panjapur, C&D waste recycling unit, Trichy Join the community of 2M+ industry professionals. Subscribe to Newsletter",
