          "description": "Saroj Poddar Group: Poddar Keventer Capital Advisors has launched a ₹400 crore real estate debt fund focused on secured investments in ultra-luxury, premium, and mid-market...",
          "articleText": "Industry 1 min read Saroj Poddar Group, Keventer launch ₹400 crore real estate debt AIF Poddar Keventer Capital Advisors has launched a Category II alternative investment fund with a target corpus of ₹400 crore and a ₹200 crore greenshoe option. The fund will invest in secured real estate debt opportunities across Delhi-NCR and West Bengal. Online Bureau ETRealty Published On Oct 3, 2026 at 08:45 AM IST Representative AI imageNEW DELHI: Saroj Poddar Group and Keventer Group-backed Poddar Keventer Capital Advisors has launched a ₹400 crore Category II alternative investment fund (AIF) focused on secured real estate debt opportunities across Delhi-NCR and West Bengal.The Poddar Keventer Real Estate Fund – Scheme I has a greenshoe option of ₹200 crore, taking its potential corpus to ₹600 crore. The sponsors have committed ₹80 crore, equivalent to 20% of the target corpus.The fund is targeting a gross internal rate of return (IRR) of 18-22% before expenses, according to the company.It plans to provide structured financing to ultra-luxury, premium and mid-market real estate projects. Investments will be structured through secured debt with security cover, escrow mechanisms, covenants and milestone-linked disbursements. By Online Bureau , ETRealty Published On Oct 3, 2026 at 08:45 AM IST See more on: Saroj Poddar Group, Keventer Group, Poddar Keventer Capital Advisors, Poddar Keventer Real Estate Fund, Category II alternative investment fund, Delhi-NCR, West Bengal Join the community of 2M+ industry professionals. Subscribe to Newsletter to get latest insights & analysis in your inbox. All about ETRealty industry right on your smartphone! Download the ETRealty App and get the Realtime updates and Save your favourite articles. HomeNewsIndustrySaroj Poddar Group, Keventer launch ₹400 crore real estate debt AIF Industry 1 min read Saroj Poddar Group, Keventer launch ₹400 crore real estate debt AIF Poddar Keventer Capital Advisors has launched a Cate