          "title": "Uttarakhand GST department recovers ₹2.25 crore as tax evasion from Eden Senior Living & Wellness",
          "description": "Uttarakhand GST SIB recovered Rs 2.25 crore from Eden Senior Living after inspection found alleged GST irregularities on flat sales; total liability Rs 12.5 crore.",
          "articleText": "Regulatory 1 min read Uttarakhand GST department recovers ₹2.25 crore as tax evasion from Eden Senior Living & Wellness Following a thorough inspection of Eden Senior Living & Wellness by the Uttarakhand tax department, it became evident that discrepancies in GST payments had occurred. The company responded by depositing Rs 2.25 crore towards its identified tax liability of Rs 12.50 crore, mainly stemming from improper input tax credit usage. Pankul Sharma TNN Published On Oct 3, 2026 at 10:47 AM IST DEHRADUN: Uttarakhand tax department has recovered Rs 2.25 crore from Eden Senior Living & Wellness, a private real estate and wellness company operating an assisted-living facility for senior citizens, after alleged irregularities were detected in the payment of GST on flat sales, officials said.Special Investigation Branch (SIB) of the department inspected the company’s premises on Thursday, with the survey continuing on Friday. Officials said the company had discharged its GST liability on the sale of flats by using input tax credit (ITC) claimed on construction-related purchases, instead of paying the liability in cash. Advt The department assessed the company’s total tax liability at Rs 12.50 crore, following which the company deposited Rs 2.25 crore in the state exchequer and its directors sought time to pay the remaining amount.Deputy commissioner Suresh Kumar told TOI that the company was not legally permitted to use ITC for the liability in question. “To substantiate the irregularities, the investigating team collected documents, forms and information from Real Estate Regulatory Authority (RERA), Mussoorie Dehradun Development Authority (MDDA), district magistrate’s office, mining section and other departments,” Kumar said, adding that the team also seized records relating to the company’s business activities.Based on an analysis of data available on the GST portal and the documents collected during the inspection, the company’s directors, legal advisers and other representatives present during the investigation admitted to the tax-payment error, Kumar said.The investigation team included deputy commissioner Suresh Kumar, assistant commissioner Krishna Kumar and officials TR Chinyal, Alisha Bisht, Kanchan Thapa and Asad Ahmed.Eden Senior Living and Wellness, located in Purkul, offers studio, one-bedroom and two-bedroom apartments for senior citizens. By Pankul Sharma , TNN Published On Oct 3, 2026 at 10:47 AM IST See more on: Uttarakhand GST department, Eden Senior Living & Wellness, Dehradun, GST evasion, input tax credit (ITC), Special Investigation Branch (SIB), RERA, Mussoorie Dehradun Development Authority (MDDA) Join the community of 2M+ industry professionals. Subscribe to Newsletter to get latest insights & analysis in your inbox. All about ETRealty industry right on your smartphone! Download the ETRealty App and get the Realtime updates and Save your favourite articles. HomeNewsRegulatoryUttarakhand GST department recovers ₹2.25 crore as tax evasion from Eden Senior Living & Wellness Regulatory 1 min read Uttarakhand GST department recovers ₹2.25 crore as tax evasion from Eden Senior Living & Wellness Following a thorough inspection of Eden Senior Living & Wellness by the Uttarakhand tax department, it became evident that discrepancies in GST payments had occurred. The company responded by depositing Rs 2.25 crore towards its identified tax liability of Rs 12.50 crore, mainly stemming from improper input tax credit usage. Regulatory 1 min read Pankul Sharma TNN Published On Oct 3, 2026 at 10:47 AM IST DEHRADUN: Uttarakhand tax department has recovered Rs 2.25 crore from Eden Senior Living & Wellness, a private real estate and wellness company operating an assisted-living facility for senior citizens, after alleged irregularities were detected in the payment of GST on flat sales, officials said.Special Investigation Branch (SIB) of the department inspected the company’s premises on Thursd