          "title": "New procurement model required for drones, new age tech adoption: ZUPPA MD Sai Pattabiram",
          "description": "Sai Pattabiram shares with us what were the learnings from Operation Sindoor and how India’s drone procurement processes can be reformed so that new age sta..",
          "articleText": "New procurement model required for drones, new age tech adoption: ZUPPA MD Sai Pattabiram In a new episode of ET Infra’s AVIATION CONNECT, Sai Pattabiram, Founder and Managing Director of ZUPPA Geo Navigation Technologies, a company which specialises in developing cutting-edge drones and autopilot systems, talks about how the future battlefield landscape will shape out and how autonomous drones have emerged as a major force vector in conflicts across the globe. Dev Kachari ETInfra Updated On Aug 13, 2026 at 05:26 PM IST Sai Pattabiram shares with us what were the learnings from Operation Sindoor and how India’s drone procurement processes can be reformed so that new age startups get a level playing field. The company’s primary client is the Indian Army and it provides specialised drones, unmanned systems, vision guidance systems, and edge computing services.He highlighted that the current defence procurement model (focused on large, capital-intensive equipment) is ill-suited for procuring new-age, technology-intensive items like drones, AI, and ML from startups. He advocates that a two-stream procurement process is needed, one for traditional equipment and another for new-age technology companies.‘Future of Warfare’ according to Pattabiram with respect to drones is shifting from \"one drone to one operator\" to \"multiple drones to one operator,\" requiring India to be prepared for swarm incursions within the next year.ZUPPA Geo Navigation Technologies is not just a drone developer, but is a technology-centric company, developing proprietary computing architecture for secure unmanned aerial systems, which is designed to avoid hacking by an adversarial force. Zuppa focuses on an indigenous computing architecture for drones, emphasising that a drone is fundamentally an edge AI computer, not just an aircraft. It performs real-time, decision-making computations based on sensor inputs, replacing human pilots. Advertisement See more on: operation