          "title": "Merlinhawk Aerospace to boost composite design through new JV: R Ramachandra Rao",
          "description": "In a new episode of ET Infra’s AVIATION CONNECT, R Ramachandra Rao, Founder and Managing Director, Merlinhawk Aerospace Pvt Ltd, joins us to highlight compo..",
          "articleText": "Merlinhawk Aerospace to boost composite design through new JV: R Ramachandra Rao In a new episode of ET Infra’s AVIATION CONNECT, R Ramachandra Rao, Founder and Managing Director, Merlinhawk Aerospace Pvt Ltd, joins us to highlight composite design and manufacturing capabilities in the country and its application in the defense and aerospace industry. Composite materials such as carbon and glass fiber reinforced polymer are now critical components used in the aerospace and defense industry which are essential for providing structural strength, durability. India’s Merlinhawk Aerospace and Italy’s Vega Composites have formed a JV for advanced composites manufacturing at Shoolagiri in the Tamil Nadu Defence Industrial Corridor. The joint venture is an outcome of Merlinhawk Aerospace’s past relationship with an Italian company Pasquali Microwave Systems, the parent company of Vega Composites. The JV aims to bring both manufacturing and, critically, design technology for composites into India, addressing a current gap where design capabilities are largely restricted to government agencies like the Department of Space, Hindustan Aeronautics Ltd, and DRDO. The new company will focus on developing high-end composites for defence, aerospace, and space applications including development of composites for the drone sector as well as explore composite technologies which if needed can find applications in the development of 5th generation or stealth fighter aircraft. The setting up of the joint venture was supported by both the Indian and Italian governments to enhance technology collaborations. Rao highlighted that setting up of defence industrial corridors, is enabling to foster an essential ecosystem including subcontractors, vendors, supply chain, test facilities, and trained manpower, which is vital for enhancing manufacturing capabilities and accelerating development cycles. He emphasised that the last 5-7 years, driven by the Government of India's \"Make in India\" policies and policy changes, have created a \"golden age\" for the defence and aerospace sector, generating substantial business. Dev Kachari ETInfra Updated On Jul 15, 2026 at 09:09 PM IST Watched by 291 Professionals Advertisement See more on: etinfra, aviation, merlinhawkaerospace, composites, italy, defence, aerospace, Join the community of 2M+ industry professionals. Subscribe to Newsletter to get latest insights & analysis in your inbox. All about ETInfra industry right on your smartphone! Download the ETInfra App and get the Realtime updates and Save your favourite articles. HomeVideosMerlinhawk Aerospace to boost composite design through new JV: R Ramachandra Rao Merlinhawk Aerospace to boost composite design through new JV: R Ramachandra Rao In a new episode of ET Infra’s AVIATION CONNECT, R Ramachandra Rao, Founder and Managing Director, Merlinhawk Aerospace Pvt Ltd, joins us to highlight composite design and manufacturing capabilities in the country and its application in the defense and aerospace industry. Composite materials such as carbon and glass fiber reinforced polymer are now critical components used in the aerospace and defense industry which are essential for providing structural strength, durability. India’s Merlinhawk Aerospace and Italy’s Vega Composites have formed a JV for advanced composites manufacturing at Shoolagiri in the Tamil Nadu Defence Industrial Corridor. The joint venture is an outcome of Merlinhawk Aerospace’s past relationship with an Italian company Pasquali Microwave Systems, the parent company of Vega Composites. The JV aims to bring both manufacturing and, critically, design technology for composites into India, addressing a current gap where design capabilities are largely restricted to government agencies like the Department of Space, Hindustan Aeronautics Ltd, and DRDO. The new company will focus on developing high-end composites for defence, aerospace, and space applications including development of