          "articleText": "Startups 1 min read Crib App acquires CirclePe Crib App has acquired rent financing company CirclePe to integrate deposit-free renting and upfront operator financing into its property management platform. CirclePe had raised about ₹7.5 crore in May 2024 at a valuation of around ₹35 crore. Online Bureau ETRealty Published On Jul 1, 2026 at 12:30 PM IST NEW DELHI: Crib App, a property management platform for co-living spaces, hostels and paying guest accommodations, has acquired CirclePe, a rent financing company.The acquisition will allow Crib to integrate rental financing into its platform, enabling tenants to move in without an upfront deposit while operators receive rent and deposit-linked financing upfront.CirclePe was founded by Navan Jaiswal and Ankur Yadav. In May 2024, the company had raised about ₹7.5 crore in a pre-seed funding round at a valuation of around ₹35 crore.It partners with non-banking financial companies to finance deposit or rent commitments. The amount is disbursed upfront to the operator, while the tenant repays in smaller monthly instalments. Advt Sunny Garg, co-founder and CEO, Crib said the integration will allow tenants to move in with zero deposit and operators to get paid upfront on the same platform. By Online Bureau , ETRealty Published On Jul 1, 2026 at 12:30 PM IST See more on: Crib App, CirclePe, property management platform, rent financing, co-living spaces, Bengaluru Join the community of 2M+ industry professionals. Subscribe to Newsletter to get latest insights & analysis in your inbox. All about ETRealty industry right on your smartphone! Download the ETRealty App and get the Realtime updates and Save your favourite articles. HomeNewsStartupsCrib App acquires CirclePe Startups 1 min read Crib App acquires CirclePe Crib App has acquired rent financing company CirclePe to integrate deposit-free renting and upfront operator financing into its property management platform. CirclePe had raised about ₹7.5 cr