          "articleText": "Startups 1 min read India Accelerator to invest $5 million to double footprint in next 12-18 months India Accelerator is set to invest $5 million to grow its coworking spaces across India. The company plans to double its presence in cities within the next 12 to 18 months. New centers are planned for Vadodara, Kolkata, Guwahati, and Bengaluru by the first half of 2026. This expansion aims to enhance community and coworking facilities nationwide. Online Bureau ETRealty Published On Mar 23, 2026 at 06:27 PM IST NEW DELHI: India Accelerator (IA) plans to invest $5 million to expand its coworking and community footprint across India. It aims to double the number of cities over the next 12-18 months.The company currently has a presence across over 20 cities, with 29 centres currently operational.In the January-March 2026 quarter, it added centers in Dehradun, Rajkot, and Vishakhapatnam.The company has plans to expand in Vadodara, Kolkata, Guwahati, and Bengaluru by H1 2026. By Online Bureau , ETRealty Published On Mar 23, 2026 at 06:27 PM IST See more on: India Accelerator, Dehradun, Rajkot, Visakhapatnam, Co-working spaces Join the community of 2M+ industry professionals. Subscribe to Newsletter to get latest insights & analysis in your inbox. All about ETRealty industry right on your smartphone! Download the ETRealty App and get the Realtime updates and Save your favourite articles. HomeNewsStartupsIndia Accelerator to invest $5 million to double footprint in next 12-18 months Startups 1 min read India Accelerator to invest $5 million to double footprint in next 12-18 months India Accelerator is set to invest $5 million to grow its coworking spaces across India. The company plans to double its presence in cities within the next 12 to 18 months. New centers are planned for Vadodara, Kolkata, Guwahati, and Bengaluru by the first half of 2026. This expansion aims to enhance community and coworking facilities nationwide. Startups 1 min read Online 