          "description": "Find answers to common queries before and after purchasing a property with Eldeco Group. Explore clear, expert‑backed FAQs for a seamless real estate buying experience.",
          "articleText": "Pre / Post Purchase FAQ's When will my Maintenance period start? The maintenance period will commence on the actual date of physical possession of the subject Unit, or on the date mentioned in the Final Demand Notice, whichever is earlier. What all documents do I/We need to carry to site at the time of taking physical possession of the Unit? In case either of the Allottees (authorised signatory in case of a partnership firm or a company) takes physical possession of the Unit, they need to carry the original possession certificate/letter & car parking usage letter, and storage/utility space usage letter issued by the Company. (P.N. If you are authorising family members/friends to take physical possession of the unit, then they have to carry the original letter of authority to the site along with the aforementioned documents.) Disclaimer: The FAQs and the answers are general guidelines for Eldeco projects. Different projects may use systems different from those explained herein. The allottee is requested to contact the concerned Customer Care executive to obtain the specific details for the project and the relevant units. Can I/We authorize someone to take physical possession/keys of my/our unit on my/our behalf? You can authorise your family members to take physical possession of the Unit on your behalf by executing the letter of authority as per the attached format in his/her name. Download format of letter of authority..doc Download format of letter of authority. What are the likely Stamp duty charges on Sale/Sublease Deed? Stamp Duty is payable on the consideration of the Unit or at the prevailing circle rate of the unit (notified by the competent authority of the state in which the unit is located), whichever is higher, at the stamp duty rates prevailing on the date on which registration of the Sale/Transfer/Conveyance deed will be executed. The stamp duty amount does not include the registration fee, which will be intimated in the Final demand notice. The Stamp Duty rates may be revised by the competent authority. What documents do I/We need to submit in case I/We wish to mortgage the Unit? Please submit the following documents for the issuance of loan documents for your unit: Signed request letter from all the allottees conveying the name of the Loaning Institution, the branch you wish to take a loan from and its address. One original set of Allotment Certificate & Agreement, duly signed by all the allottees on all pages, if not submitted earlier. Self-attested photocopy of the Pan Card of the allottees, if not submitted earlier. Please Note: The signed TPA (Tri-Party Agreement) and NOC/Permission to Mortgage (PTM) will be forwarded only after receipt of the above documents. A photocopy of the TPA, signed by all the allottee/s and stamped by the bank on all pages, needs to be sent to the company for its future reference & records. What documents do I/We need to carry along for registration of the Unit on the date of registry? The documents required at the time of Registration of the Sublease/Conveyance Deed are as follows: Indian Residents: 4 passport-size photographs for each of the allottees Passport/Photo ID proof in original Copy of PAN Card Signature & photo attestation for all the allottees from the bank Hindu Undivided Family: Copy of PAN Card of HUF 4 passport-size photographs of the authorised signatory Signature & photo attestation for all the allottees from the bank Partnership Firm: Copy of PAN Card of the Partnership Firm Notarised photocopy of Partnership Deed 4 passport-size photographs of all the partners Signature & photo attestation for all partners from the bank Company: Copy of the PAN Card of the Company Attested photocopy of the MOA of the Company Board resolution authorising the signatory to sign the documents related to the purchase and registration of property on behalf of the Company List of Directors and Shareholders of the Company 4 passport-size photographs of the authorised signatory Signature & photo attestation for the signing authority for the company from the bank Can I/we give Power of attorney (POA) for the execution of the registry &/or for signing possession documents on my/our behalf? In case you are in India, you can authorise your spouse/blood relative to execute the registry &/or sign possession documents on your behalf by executing the Power of Attorney in his/her/their name: Prepare the POA (to be downloaded from the link below) on Rs. 100/- non-judicial stamp paper purchased in the name of the executants of the POA. The duly completed POA (without blanks or handwritten text) must be signed by all executors on all pages. The POA needs to be registered either at the registrar/sub-registrar office where the executants/s inhabit or at the office of the registrar/sub-registrar where the project in which the subject unit is located is registered. The POA holder must carry the original POA to the registry. A notarised photocopy of the POA must be submitted to the C",
