ange. Kotak Alternate Asset Managers invested INR 1,200 crore in the company last year.Read more 6 hours ago Sundaram Home Finance is expanding its Emerging Business (EB) operations across smaller towns in Tamil Nadu, targeting nearly INR 200 crore in disbursements from central Tamil Nadu this year. The company opened a new EB branch in Mannargudi on September 25 and plans further branches in Karaikkal and Thiruthuraipoondi. It currently operates nearly 25 EB branches in central Tamil Nadu, alongside a wider network across Tamil Nadu, Karnataka, Andhra Pradesh and Telangana. The lender also expanded its EB presence in Andhra Pradesh this month by opening branches in Adoni, Yemminganur and Amalapuram. The EB segment covers working capital loans of up to INR 20 lakh and affordable housing finance of up to INR 40 lakh. In the first quarter, the company reported net profit of INR 85 crore on disbursements of INR 1,665 crore.Read more 10 hours ago India’s top seven office markets recorded 54.4 million sq ft of Grade A leasing during January-September 2026, a 7% year-on-year increase, according to Colliers India. Quarterly leasing reached 18.7 million sq ft in Q3, rising 7% from Q2 and 9% from the corresponding quarter last year. Bengaluru remained the largest market with 15.7 million sq ft of leasing during the nine-month period, while Hyderabad recorded a 47% annual increase to 9.4 million sq ft. Flex space operators accounted for 12.6 million sq ft, or 23% of total leasing, with demand rising 37% year-on-year. Technology companies remained the largest conventional occupiers, followed by BFSI and engineering and manufacturing firms. New supply increased marginally to 41.7 million sq ft, despite record quarterly completions of 19.2 million sq ft in Q3.Read more Advertisement The Gulf conflict has disrupted global supply chains, pushed... REITs have changed the way commercial real estate is owned a... What really powers the cloud? Behind every Google search, A... What rea