          "title": "Mokila transforms into luxury villa hub",
          "description": "Mokila is emerging as a prominent villa destination in western Hyderabad, driven by demand for larger homes, gated communities and improving connectivity.",
          "articleText": "Large homes, gated communities and western connectivity drive new demand Property Pulse Hyderabad’s real estate growth has steadily moved westward from established locations such as Gachibowli, Madhapur and Kondapur. After Kokapet, Narsingi and Gandipet, Mokila is now gaining a distinct identity as a residential destination, particularly for buyers seeking larger homes and villas. Located away from the city’s dense urban core, Mokila offers larger land parcels, relatively quieter surroundings and growing gated communities. The combination is attracting both developers and homebuyers looking for spacious, premium residences. Mokila was once largely viewed as a peripheral location. That is changing as villa communities and premium residential projects take shape across the area. Developments featuring duplex and independent villas, landscaped open spaces, clubhouses and security facilities are expanding the area’s residential profile. The market is attracting professionals and business families who want more space and privacy than conventional apartment living offers. The availability of larger parcels suitable for low-density developments is also giving Mokila an advantage in the villa segment. Connectivity is becoming an important factor in Mokila’s growth. The area is linked to western Hyderabad through Shankarpally Road, with road access towards Gandipet, Narsingi, Kokapet and the Financial District. Connections to the Outer Ring Road network further improve access to employment and commercial centres. As office and business activity expands across western Hyderabad, residential development is also spreading into locations beyond the established IT corridor. Mokila’s growth is therefore part of a larger western corridor that includes Shankarpally, Gandipet, Manchirevula, Khanapur, Narsingi and Kokapet. Villas remain the defining feature of Mokila’s residential market, but prices vary significantly between projects. Plot size, built-up area, location, road access, construction quality, amenities, community infrastructure and project approvals can all influence the final price. Advertised prices therefore do not necessarily provide a complete picture of the cost of ownership. Buyers also need to account for additional charges and compare actual transaction values across projects before making a purchase decision. Villa prices in Mokila are currently reported to range from around ₹3.5 crore to more than ₹20 crore, depending on the project, size and specifications. Some 3 BHK villas are positioned around the ₹3.5–4 crore range, while 4 BHK homes can range from approximately ₹4.5 crore to above ₹6 crore. Larger luxury villas in premium gated communities can command ₹7 crore or more, with some properties crossing ₹20 crore. The wide range reflects the diversity of projects entering the market rather than a single benchmark for the locality. VILLA SHIFT.",
          "newsLink": "https://proppuls.in/mokila-villas-western-hyderabad-luxury-homes-connectivity",
