          "title": "SPR Infrastructure 2026: Live Road & Metro Status",
          "description": "The latest verified status of SPR's infrastructure - elevated corridor, metro proposal and road upgrades - planned, tendered and under construction.",
          "articleText": "Last Verified: August 2026This page is updated as project status changes. Before making a purchase decision based on any infrastructure project, buyers should cross-check the latest information with GMDA’s official announcements and Haryana’s e-procurement portal. Table of Contents Toggle Featured Projects More projects → BPTP GAIA Residences Gurugram, Haryana From ₹38,500,000 Godrej Alira Gurugram, Haryana From ₹60,000,000 Signature Global Cloverdale SPR Gurugram, Haryana From ₹38,799,997 Quick AnswerSouthern Peripheral Road has several infrastructure projects at different stages, but none of its major projects are under construction as of August 2026. As a homebuyer, you need to be aware of what is happening in this corridor.The ₹755 crore tender for the Vatika Chowk to NH-48 elevated corridor was cancelled on June 4, 2026, while the Ghata Chowk to Vatika Chowk elevated stretch is back at the DPR stage. The proposed Sector 56 to Pachgaon metro has progressed further, with its DPR cleared by the HMRTC board and submitted to the Haryana government in July 2026, but construction has not started.A smaller road-improvement project between Vatika Chowk and Ghata Chowk is currently the most advanced infrastructure work associated with SPR.For buyers, the key point is simple:Proposed, approved, tendered, under construction and operational are not the same thing.SPR Infrastructure Status at a GlanceProjectScopeCurrent StatusEstimated CostVatika Chowk to NH-48 elevated corridor4.2 km, 4+4 lanesTender cancelled June 4, 2026; fresh procurement required₹755 croreGhata Chowk to Vatika Chowk elevated stretch6 km, part of a larger 12-km route to NH-8DPR and planning stageNot finalisedVatika Chowk to Ghata Chowk road improvementsShoulder paving and surface upgradesImprovement works planned; most advanced project currently in motion₹5.5 to ₹6.5 croreSector 56 to Pachgaon metroApproximately 35 km, 28 elevated stationsDPR cleared by HMRTC board and submitted to Haryana government; construction not startedApproximately ₹8,500 croreHUDA City Centre to Cyber City metro extensionSeparate line, partly along the corridorPlanned, but less advanced than Sector 56 to PachgaonNot finalisedThe current project stages are based on the updated SPR infrastructure tracker.What Do the Different Statuses Mean?When evaluating infrastructure claims, buyers should distinguish between the following:Proposed: The project has been identified or discussed but has not cleared the necessary planning or approval stages. Approved: The relevant authority has approved the project or a particular stage. Construction may still be some way off. DPR stage: A Detailed Project Report is being prepared, reviewed or finalised. Tendered: Contractors have been invited to bid. A tender does not mean construction has started. Under construction: A contractor has been appointed and physical work has begun. Operational: The infrastructure is complete and available for public use.As of August 2026, none of SPR’s major infrastructure projects have reached the last two stages.What Changed on SPR in 2026?The year has seen significant movement, but not all of it has been forward.In March 2026, GMDA floated a ₹755 crore tender for the 4.2-km Vatika Chowk to NH-48 elevated corridor.In June, that tender was formally cancelled. GMDA also began the process of appointing a consultant for a fresh DPR covering the Ghata Chowk to Vatika Chowk stretch.The Sector 56 to Pachgaon metro followed a different trajectory. Its DPR cleared the HMRTC board in June and was submitted to the Haryana government in July for further approval.The result is a fragmented infrastructure picture:The elevated-road projects have faced delays and procurement changes, while the metro proposal has continued to progress through its planning stages.These should therefore be evaluated as separate projects, not as one broad promise of “upcoming SPR infrastructure.”What About the ₹2,000 Crore SPR Allocation?Haryana’s 2025-26 budget allocated approximately ₹2,000 crore towards SPR infrastructure upgrades.This demonstrates government focus on the corridor, but a budget allocation should not be interpreted as proof that every project is funded, tendered or under construction.The cancellation of the Vatika Chowk to NH-48 tender is a useful reminder that a budgetary commitment does not automatically translate into physical construction.What Should Buyers Check?If infrastructure is influencing your property decision, ask five questions:1. Which project actually affects this property?Identify the exact stretch, rather than relying on a general reference to “SPR infrastructure.”2. What stage is it at?Is it proposed, approved, at DPR stage, tendered or under construction?3. Has a contractor been appointed?A floated tender is not the same as physical work.4. Where did the completion date come from?Check whether it is based on an official GMDA or HMRTC statement or simply a marketing estimate.5. Would you still buy if the pr",
